# Fontconfig parses its XML configuration once per process and keeps global
# state alive until exit; LeakSanitizer flags those one-time init allocations
# (fontconfig -> expat XML_ParseBuffer) on systems where the parse allocates
# lazily (seen on Ubuntu 26.04, not on Arch). Not our memory -- suppress the
# whole library, since the system .so is stripped and symbol-level entries
# would not match.
leak:libfontconfig
